@page
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Working with Work — Guide";
}
<div class="page-header">
    <div class="section-head section-head--plain">
        <h1>Working with Work</h1>
        <p class="page-context">Create, assign, update and resolve operational work.</p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="zone">
    <div class="guide-flow">
        <div class="guide-flow__step">Create</div>
        <span class="guide-flow__arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
        <div class="guide-flow__step">Classify</div>
        <span class="guide-flow__arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
        <div class="guide-flow__step">Assign</div>
        <span class="guide-flow__arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
        <div class="guide-flow__step">Work</div>
        <span class="guide-flow__arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
        <div class="guide-flow__step">Resolve</div>
    </div>

    <div class="guide-term-grid">
        <div class="guide-term">
            <p class="guide-term__name">Create</p>
            <p class="guide-term__body">Describe the work, then route it to the team that owns it. A title, a description, a team and a category are required.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="guide-term">
            <p class="guide-term__name">Classify</p>
            <p class="guide-term__body">Choose a work type (Incident, Service Request, Task, Problem) and a priority (Critical, High, Medium, Low). Priority sets the SLA target.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="guide-term">
            <p class="guide-term__name">Assign</p>
            <p class="guide-term__body">A ticket moves from Open to Assigned once someone owns it. Only an active member of the ticket's own team can be assigned.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="guide-term">
            <p class="guide-term__name">Work</p>
            <p class="guide-term__body">The assignee starts work (In Progress), or puts it On Hold with a reason if it's waiting on someone else — the SLA clock pauses while it's on hold.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="guide-term">
            <p class="guide-term__name">Resolve</p>
            <p class="guide-term__body">Resolving requires a resolution and a note. A Manager or Admin (or the requester) then closes it. A closed or resolved ticket can be reopened if the work isn't actually done.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <p class="prose">
        Every change — assignment, status, priority, comments — is recorded on the ticket's own
        activity timeline, so the history of a piece of work is always visible on its Ticket
        Detail page.
    </p>

    <p class="page-actions">
        <a class="btn-primary" asp-page="/Tickets/Create">Create work</a>
        <a class="btn" asp-page="/Tickets/Index">Open Work Queue</a>
    </p>
</div>

<div class="guide-section-nav">
    <a class="back-link" asp-page="/Guide/Index">&larr; Back to Guide</a>
</div>
